---
/**
 * The safety disclaimer required on every calculator page by section 4.3
 * rule 7: above the fold, in the results area, plain language, calm.
 *
 * Deliberately not styled as a warning. No icon, no border, no amber. It is a
 * statement of what the number is, placed where someone reading the number will
 * see it — not an alert that trains people to skip it.
 *
 * The second sentence is the signposting the rule requires. It is one line and
 * non-directive: it names where to take a concern without implying the reader
 * has one.
 */
---

<p class="mt-4 max-w-[var(--measure)] text-xs text-graphite">
  These are estimates from population-level equations, and individual needs vary — this is not
  medical advice. If you have concerns about eating, weight or body image, a doctor or a qualified
  professional is the right place to take them.
</p>
